# Copy to /etc/homelab-monitor/backend.env and chmod 600 - sessions are
# stored in the database this points at, so keep it private.

# SQLite database for user accounts and sessions. Created on first start;
# the seed command must be run before the backend will start:
#   go run ./cmd/backend seed
# Sessions are stored here too, so keep the file private (it is chmod 0600
# automatically).
HOMELAB_DB_FILE=data/homelab.db

# Add the Secure flag to the session cookie. Enable ONLY when serving over
# HTTPS (e.g. behind a reverse proxy) - on plain HTTP it would break login.
# HOMELAB_COOKIE_SECURE=1

# Optional - see README.md for the full list and defaults.
# HOMELAB_AGENTS=192.168.1.10:8080,192.168.1.11:8080  (only the initial seed - see HOMELAB_AGENTS_FILE)
# HOMELAB_AGENTS_FILE=data/agents.json
# HOMELAB_POLL_INTERVAL=5
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
# DISCORD_ALERT_THRESHOLD=2
# HOMELAB_CPU_THRESHOLD=90
# HOMELAB_MEM_THRESHOLD=90
# HOMELAB_DISK_THRESHOLD=90

# Listen address. Default :9090; set HOMELAB_PORT to run multiple instances
# (dev/test) side by side without port collisions.
# HOMELAB_PORT=9090

# Sent as X-Homelab-Agent-Token on every poll (and every restart relay).
# Must match HOMELAB_AGENT_TOKEN in each agent's own env exactly - same
# value, same env var name. Leave unset to poll agents unauthenticated
# (the default).
# HOMELAB_AGENT_TOKEN=

# Restart commands live in each AGENT's own HOMELAB_ACTIONS (see
# deploy/agent.env.example) - the agent re-validates restart requests
# against its own config and never runs a command received over the wire.
# This var is accepted here as documentation only; the backend does not use
# it. Leave it unset.
# HOMELAB_ACTIONS=
